        <mxCell id="interpretation-box" value="LIME provides local explanations for individual predictions, showing which molecular features (e.g., hydrogen bond acceptors, rotatable bonds) contribute most to a specific prediction. SHAP provides global feature importance across all predictions, revealing that lipophilicity (logP) is the most influential feature overall. Together, these methods provide both instance-specific and model-wide interpretability, enabling understanding of both individual predictions and overall model behavior." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontColor=#000000;strokeWidth=1.5;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1">
